WEBVTT

00:02.467 --> 00:04.052
KATARA: Water...

00:04.886 --> 00:06.346
Earth...

00:06.888 --> 00:08.515
Fire...

00:08.973 --> 00:10.225
Air.

00:11.226 --> 00:14.646
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.355 --> 00:18.816
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.734 --> 00:22.570
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:22.654 --> 00:23.738
could stop them.

00:23.821 --> 00:25.490
But when the world
needed him most,

00:25.573 --> 00:26.741
he vanished.

00:27.367 --> 00:28.785
100 years passed,

00:28.868 --> 00:31.120
and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar―

00:31.371 --> 00:32.872
An airbender named Aang.

00:32.956 --> 00:35.083
And although his airbending
skills are great,

00:35.166 --> 00:38.002
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:38.086 --> 00:39.087
AANG: Oof.

00:39.170 --> 00:42.298
But I believe Aang
can save the world.

00:51.724 --> 00:53.476
ZHAO: I discovered a hidden library.

00:54.018 --> 00:56.896
I tore through
scroll after scroll.

00:59.941 --> 01:01.067
TOPH: You did it!

01:01.359 --> 01:02.485
You're an earthbender.

01:03.069 --> 01:06.573
ROKU: Sozin's Comet will return
by the end of the summer.

01:06.656 --> 01:10.410
And Fire Lord Ozai will use
its power to finish the war

01:10.493 --> 01:11.911
once and for all.

01:12.370 --> 01:14.706
You must defeat the Fire Lord

01:14.789 --> 01:16.708
before the comet arrives.

01:26.509 --> 01:27.635
SOKKA: What's out here?

01:27.885 --> 01:30.513
TOPH: A lot, actually.
There's hundreds of little―

01:30.597 --> 01:32.682
Shh! I know you
can see underground,

01:32.765 --> 01:34.434
but don't ruin the surprise.

01:34.517 --> 01:35.810
Just watch.

01:36.227 --> 01:37.228
♪♪
♪♪

01:37.312 --> 01:38.438
♪ Eh ♪

01:38.521 --> 01:39.731
Ha ha! Yeah!

01:40.106 --> 01:41.357
♪♪
♪♪

01:41.441 --> 01:42.442
♪ Eh! ♪

01:42.525 --> 01:44.235
I'm putting
an orchestra together.

01:44.319 --> 01:45.653
Orchestra, huh? Well...

01:45.737 --> 01:47.280
♪ La-di-da ♪

01:47.572 --> 01:49.115
-♪ Laah ♪
-♪ Diih ♪

01:49.240 --> 01:50.241
♪ Daah ♪

01:52.744 --> 01:53.745
♪♪
♪♪

01:53.828 --> 01:54.829
♪ Eh ♪

01:54.912 --> 01:55.955
♪ Eh! ♪

01:56.039 --> 01:57.040
♪ Eh! ♪

01:57.123 --> 01:58.291
♪ Eh ♪

01:59.292 --> 02:00.376
This is great and all,

02:00.460 --> 02:03.046
But don't we have more important things
to worry about?

02:03.129 --> 02:04.380
We should be making plans.

02:04.714 --> 02:06.174
We did make plans.

02:06.257 --> 02:07.884
We're all picking mini-vacations.

02:08.176 --> 02:10.053
There's no time for vacations.

02:10.345 --> 02:12.347
I'm learning the elements
as fast as I can.

02:12.555 --> 02:15.475
I practice hard every day
with Toph and Katara.

02:15.558 --> 02:17.101
I've been training
my arrow off.

02:17.477 --> 02:20.688
Yeah. What's wrong with having a little
fun in our downtime?

02:20.772 --> 02:23.399
Even if you do master all of
the elements, then what?

02:23.483 --> 02:25.693
It's not like we have
a map of the Fire Nation.

02:25.777 --> 02:28.696
Should we just head west
until we reach the Fire Lord's house?

02:28.780 --> 02:31.616
Knock, knock! Hello, Fire Lord!
Anybody home?

02:31.699 --> 02:32.950
I don't think so.

02:33.034 --> 02:35.578
We need some intelligence
if we're gonna win this war.

02:35.662 --> 02:36.663
♪ Laah ♪

02:36.746 --> 02:39.332
Hee hee! All right.
We'll finish our vacations.

02:39.415 --> 02:41.626
And then we'll look
for Sokka's intelligence.

02:43.127 --> 02:44.504
AANG: Your turn, Katara.

02:44.587 --> 02:46.881
Where would you
like to go on your mini-vacation?

02:46.964 --> 02:49.384
How about
the Misty Palms Oasis?

02:49.467 --> 02:50.593
That sounds refreshing.

02:50.677 --> 02:53.596
Oh, yeah, I've been there.
It's a pristine natural ice spring.

02:53.680 --> 02:56.099
And I don't usually
use the word "pristine."

02:56.182 --> 02:58.267
It's one of
nature's wonders.

02:58.351 --> 02:59.852
( SOUNDTRACK MUSIC SLOWS DOWN )

03:00.395 --> 03:03.690
Must have changed
ownership since I was here.

03:03.773 --> 03:05.233
Heh heh.

03:15.284 --> 03:16.452
Ptooey!

03:18.496 --> 03:19.789
( GROWLING )

03:25.712 --> 03:27.255
( SNORING )

03:27.338 --> 03:28.965
One mango, please.

03:42.895 --> 03:44.397
I don't see anything wrong

03:44.480 --> 03:46.691
with having one of those
fruity beverages

03:46.774 --> 03:48.735
while we plan our strategy.

03:49.819 --> 03:50.903
Excuse me.

03:54.240 --> 03:56.159
No worries. I clean up easy.

03:59.036 --> 04:00.413
You're a living relic.

04:00.496 --> 04:01.998
Thanks. I try.

04:02.081 --> 04:05.126
An Air Nomad right front of me.

04:05.209 --> 04:06.919
Professor Zei,
head of anthropology

04:07.003 --> 04:08.671
at Ba Sing Se University.

04:08.963 --> 04:10.089
Tell me...

04:10.173 --> 04:13.134
Which of the air temples
do you hail from?

04:13.217 --> 04:14.343
The Southern Temple.

04:14.427 --> 04:16.763
Oh, splendid! Now, tell me,

04:16.846 --> 04:19.640
what was the primary
agricultural product of your people?

04:19.724 --> 04:23.436
Uh, are fruit pies
an agricultural product?

04:23.603 --> 04:27.064
Oh! Truly fascinating.
That's one for the journal.

04:27.356 --> 04:30.568
SOKKA: So, professor,
you're obviously a well-traveled guy.

04:30.651 --> 04:32.195
Do you have a more
current map?

04:32.278 --> 04:33.780
Ours seems to be
a little dated.

04:34.363 --> 04:35.615
Certainly.

04:38.367 --> 04:40.286
What? No Fire Nation?

04:40.369 --> 04:42.789
Doesn't anybody have
a good map of that place?

04:43.039 --> 04:45.458
KATARA: You've made a lot
of trips into the desert.

04:45.541 --> 04:46.959
ZEI: All in vain, I'm afraid.

04:47.043 --> 04:50.129
I've found lost civilizations
all over the Earth Kingdom,

04:50.213 --> 04:53.800
but I haven't managed to find
the crown jewel―

04:54.258 --> 04:56.511
Wan Shi Tong's library.

04:56.928 --> 05:00.348
You've spent years
walking through the desert to find

05:00.431 --> 05:01.682
some guy's library?

05:02.016 --> 05:05.436
This library is more valuable
than gold, little lady.

05:05.520 --> 05:09.148
It is said to contain a vast collection
of knowledge.

05:09.232 --> 05:10.483
And knowledge...

05:11.067 --> 05:12.276
Is priceless.

05:12.360 --> 05:14.570
( DEADPAN ) Hmm. Sounds like good times.

05:14.862 --> 05:17.281
Oh, it is. According to legend,

05:17.365 --> 05:20.034
It was built by the great knowledge spirit

05:20.159 --> 05:24.330
Wan Shi Tong with the help
of his foxy knowledge seekers.

05:24.705 --> 05:28.084
Oh, so this spirit
has attractive assistants, huh?

05:28.167 --> 05:30.795
I think he means
they look like actual foxes, Sokka.

05:30.878 --> 05:32.171
ZEI: You're both right.

05:32.255 --> 05:33.881
Handsome little creatures.

05:33.965 --> 05:36.092
Wan Shi Tong and his knowledge seekers

05:36.175 --> 05:38.469
collected books from all over the world

05:38.553 --> 05:41.556
and put them on display
for mankind to read

05:41.639 --> 05:43.391
so that we might better ourselves.

05:43.474 --> 05:45.726
If this place has books
from all over the world,

05:45.810 --> 05:48.729
do you think they've got
info on the Fire Nation? A map maybe?

05:48.813 --> 05:49.897
I wouldn't know.

05:50.022 --> 05:52.233
But if such a thing exists,

05:52.316 --> 05:54.819
it's in Wan Shi Tong's library.

05:56.362 --> 05:59.490
Then it's settled. Aang,
I do believe it's my turn.

05:59.574 --> 06:02.577
I'd like to spend my vacation
at the library!

06:03.786 --> 06:07.081
Uh, hey, what about me?
When do I get to pick?

06:07.164 --> 06:09.000
You've got to work
here a little longer

06:09.083 --> 06:11.210
before you're qualified
for vacation time.

06:11.294 --> 06:12.295
Hmph.

06:12.378 --> 06:14.463
Of course, there's the matter
of finding it.

06:14.547 --> 06:16.799
I've made several trips
into the Zi Huang desert

06:16.883 --> 06:18.634
and almost died each time.

06:18.718 --> 06:21.846
I'm afraid that desert's
impossible to cross.

06:22.847 --> 06:25.558
Professor, would you like to see
our sky bison?

06:25.808 --> 06:29.186
A sky bison? You actually have one?!

06:29.270 --> 06:31.439
( GROWLING )

06:31.522 --> 06:34.150
Sandbenders, shoo!
Away from the bison!

06:55.922 --> 06:58.966
Tell me, sky bison,
are you the last of your breed?

07:00.217 --> 07:03.846
Oh, delightful! I only wish
I spoke his tongue.

07:03.930 --> 07:06.807
Oh, the stories this beast could tell.

07:08.142 --> 07:09.268
Shush, chatty monkey.

07:10.478 --> 07:12.063
Wow. It shouldn't be too hard

07:12.146 --> 07:13.814
to find a place like this out here.

07:18.402 --> 07:20.529
Ah! Does this place even exist?

07:20.613 --> 07:22.073
Some say it doesn't.

07:22.949 --> 07:25.618
Shouldn't you have mentioned that before?

07:25.743 --> 07:26.827
Grr!

07:32.041 --> 07:33.459
There it is!

07:37.964 --> 07:40.800
That's what it will sound like
when one of you spots it.

07:43.010 --> 07:44.136
( APPA GROWLING )

07:45.388 --> 07:48.891
It shouldn't be this hard to spot
a giant ornate building from the air.

07:52.687 --> 07:54.355
Down there. What's that?

07:59.485 --> 08:02.113
Forget it. It's obviously not
what we're looking for.

08:02.446 --> 08:04.365
The building in this
drawing is enormous.

08:13.416 --> 08:14.875
What kind of animal is that?

08:18.254 --> 08:20.673
ZEI: I think that was one
of the knowledge seekers.

08:21.173 --> 08:23.009
Oh, we must be close to the library.

08:23.467 --> 08:26.512
No. This is the library. Look!

08:29.098 --> 08:30.266
It's completely buried.

08:38.607 --> 08:40.735
ZEI: The library is buried?!

08:40.818 --> 08:43.529
My life's ambition is now full of sand.

08:44.113 --> 08:46.115
Well, time to start excavating.

08:49.618 --> 08:52.038
Actually, that won't
be necessary.

08:52.121 --> 08:54.331
The inside seems to be completely intact.

08:54.790 --> 08:56.083
And it's huge.

08:56.167 --> 08:58.419
SOKKA: That fox thingy
went in through a window.

08:58.502 --> 09:00.796
I say we climb up there
and give it a look.

09:00.880 --> 09:03.132
I say you guys
go ahead without me.

09:03.215 --> 09:05.051
You've got something
against libraries?

09:05.134 --> 09:06.844
I've held books before.

09:06.927 --> 09:08.846
And I got to tell you,

09:08.929 --> 09:10.890
they don't exactly do it for me.

09:10.973 --> 09:12.850
Oh, right. Sorry.

09:13.267 --> 09:15.770
Let me know if they have
something you can listen to.

09:20.900 --> 09:24.820
Don't worry, buddy. I'm not making you
go underground ever again.

09:24.904 --> 09:26.447
You can stay out here with Toph.

09:32.745 --> 09:33.788
What's up?

09:41.253 --> 09:42.421
( CHATTERS )

09:43.798 --> 09:45.841
ZEI: Oh, it's breathtaking.

09:46.467 --> 09:49.053
The spirit spared no expense
in designing this place.

09:49.136 --> 09:51.263
Look at those beautiful buttresses.

09:51.347 --> 09:52.723
- Hee hee!
- Hee hee!

09:52.807 --> 09:54.100
ZEI: What's funny?

09:54.183 --> 09:56.310
Nothing. We just like architecture.

09:56.811 --> 09:58.229
As do I.

10:01.148 --> 10:02.441
My word!

10:02.566 --> 10:07.446
The exquisite mosaic handiwork
of this tile-rendered avian symbol―

10:07.988 --> 10:10.574
Eh, nice owl.

10:10.658 --> 10:11.826
( RUSTLING )

10:12.618 --> 10:13.953
( CHATTERING )

10:26.382 --> 10:28.884
I know you're
back there.

10:31.554 --> 10:32.555
Hello!

10:32.638 --> 10:34.932
I'm Professor Zei, head of anthropology

10:35.015 --> 10:36.392
at Ba Sing Se University.

10:37.351 --> 10:39.812
You should leave
the way you came

10:39.895 --> 10:43.315
Unless you want
to become a stuffed head of anthropology.

10:43.399 --> 10:44.608
( SPEAKING GIBBERISH )

10:45.151 --> 10:48.279
Are you the spirit who brought
this library to the physical world?

10:48.362 --> 10:53.117
Indeed. I am Wan Shi Tong,
he who knows 10,000 things.

10:53.492 --> 10:55.244
And you are obviously humans,

10:55.661 --> 10:58.581
Which, by the way,
are no longer permitted in my study.

10:58.664 --> 11:00.499
AANG: What do you have against humans?

11:00.583 --> 11:03.752
Hmm. Humans only bother learning things

11:03.836 --> 11:05.546
to get the edge on other humans,

11:05.963 --> 11:09.508
Like that firebender who came
to this place a few years ago,

11:09.592 --> 11:11.927
looking to destroy his enemy.

11:12.386 --> 11:15.431
So who are you trying to destroy?

11:15.764 --> 11:19.977
What? No, no, no destroying.
We're not into that.

11:20.060 --> 11:22.479
WAN SHI TONG: Then why have you come here?

11:22.897 --> 11:26.525
Um, knowledge for knowledge's sake.

11:27.443 --> 11:30.905
If you're going to lie
to an all-knowing spirit being,

11:30.988 --> 11:33.115
you should at least
put some effort into it.

11:33.199 --> 11:35.534
I'm not lying! I'm here with the Avatar,

11:35.618 --> 11:38.746
And he's the bridge between our worlds.
He'll vouch for me.

11:39.121 --> 11:40.122
Ow!

11:40.581 --> 11:43.334
Uh, yeah. I'll vouch.

11:43.667 --> 11:46.670
We will not abuse the knowledge
in your library, good spirit.

11:46.754 --> 11:48.214
You have my word.

11:48.297 --> 11:53.802
Hmm. Very well.
I'll let you peruse my vast collection

11:53.886 --> 11:55.471
on one condition―

11:55.846 --> 11:57.765
To prove your worth as scholars,

11:57.848 --> 12:01.185
you have to contribute
some worthwhile knowledge.

12:02.102 --> 12:05.564
Please accept this tome
as a donation to your library.

12:06.065 --> 12:08.776
First edition. Very nice.

12:12.613 --> 12:14.615
I have an authentic waterbending scroll.

12:15.074 --> 12:18.827
Oh, these illustrations are quite stylish.

12:20.788 --> 12:22.623
Uh, oh! I know.

12:23.832 --> 12:24.833
Ha!

12:25.209 --> 12:27.086
I suppose that counts.

12:29.004 --> 12:31.840
Oh, great spirit, check this out.

12:32.132 --> 12:33.509
Ta-da!

12:34.927 --> 12:36.053
It's a special knot.

12:36.136 --> 12:37.346
That counts as knowledge.

12:38.222 --> 12:40.349
You're not very bright, are you?

12:42.518 --> 12:44.186
Enjoy the library.

12:51.360 --> 12:53.153
Bright enough to fool you.

12:56.865 --> 13:00.035
So, do you like flying?

13:02.329 --> 13:05.541
Of course, I'm more comfortable
on the ground where I can see.

13:05.624 --> 13:08.252
Well, I don't see the way you do.

13:08.627 --> 13:11.380
I feel the vibrations in the ground
with my feet.

13:11.755 --> 13:14.591
But this sand is
so loose and shifty,

13:14.675 --> 13:16.719
It makes everything look fuzzy.

13:16.802 --> 13:18.262
( GROWLS )

13:18.345 --> 13:20.514
Not that there's
anything wrong with fuzzy.

13:31.525 --> 13:33.610
Hey! Look at these
weird lion-turtle things.

13:34.903 --> 13:36.363
Ah, I've seen weirder.

13:36.447 --> 13:39.575
Aang, did you know in a past life,
you were left-handed?

13:39.658 --> 13:41.452
I always knew I was special.

13:51.503 --> 13:54.923
"The darkest day in Fire Nation history."

13:55.257 --> 13:56.592
It's got a date at the top,

13:56.675 --> 13:58.427
but it doesn't say anything else.

14:04.975 --> 14:06.810
Sokka, where are you going?

14:06.894 --> 14:10.147
I want to know what happened
to the Fire Nation on their darkest day.

14:10.230 --> 14:11.398
This could be promising.

14:13.484 --> 14:16.403
The information on the Fire Nation
should be right up here.

14:19.323 --> 14:20.449
AANG: Firebenders.

14:20.532 --> 14:23.744
KATARA: They destroyed everything
having to do with the Fire Nation.

14:24.286 --> 14:25.746
That's so unfair!

14:25.829 --> 14:28.457
Just when I think
I'm one step ahead of the Fire Nation,

14:28.540 --> 14:31.001
it turns out they beat us here
a long time ago.

14:31.752 --> 14:34.380
I need to know what happened
on the darkest day.

14:34.463 --> 14:35.964
( WHIMPERING )

14:36.715 --> 14:39.676
Hello, little weird fox guy.

14:42.137 --> 14:44.223
ZEI: It seems it's trying to assist you.

14:44.890 --> 14:48.268
Um, sure. I guess I'll follow you.

15:15.671 --> 15:19.633
This room is a true marvel,
a mechanical wonder.

15:19.716 --> 15:22.928
It's a planetarium
that shows the heavens moving.

15:25.848 --> 15:28.684
SOKKA: This is beautiful,
but how is it helpful?

15:29.226 --> 15:32.104
Maybe these dials
represent dates and times.

15:32.187 --> 15:35.065
Sokka, try entering that date
from that parchment you took.

15:35.441 --> 15:40.279
Shh! Katara, not in front of the fox.
He's with the owl.

15:40.529 --> 15:41.530
( WHIMPERS )

15:59.465 --> 16:01.925
Wow! I got to hand it to you, Sokka,

16:02.009 --> 16:04.553
You picked
the best mini-vacation for sure.

16:08.849 --> 16:10.934
KATARA: Hey, wait.
What happened to the sun?

16:11.852 --> 16:13.979
Great. You must have broken it.

16:14.354 --> 16:15.981
It's not broken.

16:17.316 --> 16:20.861
The sun is behind the moon.
It's a solar eclipse.

16:21.236 --> 16:24.281
It's literally the darkest day
in Fire Nation history.

16:24.364 --> 16:26.825
Now I get it.
Something awful happened on that day.

16:26.909 --> 16:28.702
I don't know what, but I do know why.

16:29.077 --> 16:32.831
Firebenders lose their bending
during a solar eclipse.

16:32.915 --> 16:33.957
Sorry.

16:34.041 --> 16:35.042
That makes sense.

16:35.125 --> 16:37.794
I mean, think of what the lunar eclipse
at the North Pole

16:37.878 --> 16:39.213
did to the waterbenders.

16:39.296 --> 16:40.339
This is huge.

16:40.422 --> 16:41.423
( FOX WHIMPERS )

16:43.842 --> 16:45.135
Fine. You earned it.

16:47.429 --> 16:50.557
We've got to get this information
to the Earth King at Ba Sing Se.

16:50.641 --> 16:52.184
We'll wait for the next eclipse.

16:52.267 --> 16:55.270
Then we'll invade the Fire Nation
when they're totally helpless.

16:55.354 --> 16:57.022
The Fire Lord is going down!

16:57.981 --> 17:00.317
Mortals are so predictable

17:00.776 --> 17:02.819
and such terrible liars.

17:03.529 --> 17:04.530
( SOKKA GULPS )

17:09.159 --> 17:11.036
You betrayed my trust.

17:11.411 --> 17:14.289
From the beginning,
you intended to misuse this knowledge

17:14.373 --> 17:15.791
for evil purposes.

17:16.166 --> 17:19.545
You don't understand.
If anyone's evil, it's the Fire Nation.

17:19.628 --> 17:21.463
You saw what they did to your library.

17:21.547 --> 17:23.423
They're destructive and dangerous.

17:23.507 --> 17:25.259
We need this information.

17:25.676 --> 17:29.263
You think you're the first person
to believe their war was justified?

17:29.388 --> 17:31.765
Countless others before
you have come here,

17:31.848 --> 17:34.935
seeking weapons
or weaknesses or battle strategies.

17:35.185 --> 17:38.063
We had no choice.
Please. We're just desperate to protect

17:38.146 --> 17:39.398
the people we love.

17:39.731 --> 17:43.569
And now I am going
to protect what I love.

17:47.072 --> 17:48.448
AANG: What are you doing?

17:48.865 --> 17:54.162
I'm taking my knowledge back.
No one will ever abuse it again.

17:54.413 --> 17:57.040
He's sinking the building.
We've got to get out of here!

17:57.249 --> 18:01.587
I'm afraid I can't allow that.
You already know too much.

18:01.962 --> 18:03.005
- Aah!
- Aah!

18:03.755 --> 18:05.215
( KIDS SCREAMING )

18:10.387 --> 18:11.847
( GROWLS )

18:12.180 --> 18:14.850
I already told you.
I don't want to snuggle.

18:19.563 --> 18:22.774
Library's sinking.
Library's sinking!

18:23.483 --> 18:25.027
Hyah!

18:33.452 --> 18:34.536
( YELLS )

18:51.094 --> 18:52.304
Aah!

18:53.013 --> 18:55.098
Great knowledge spirit, I beg you,

18:55.182 --> 18:59.311
do not destroy your vast collection
of priceless tomes.

19:00.854 --> 19:02.356
Aah!

19:10.656 --> 19:12.658
We've got to get back to the surface.

19:14.743 --> 19:16.078
Sokka, let's go.

19:16.411 --> 19:19.331
But we still don't know
when the next eclipse is gonna happen.

19:19.414 --> 19:21.208
Don't be stupid.
We'll find out later.

19:21.291 --> 19:23.418
No, we won't.
If we leave this place,

19:23.543 --> 19:25.087
we'll never get the information.

19:25.170 --> 19:27.756
Aang, come with me
to the planetarium. I need cover.

19:28.090 --> 19:29.925
Katara, take Momo and get out of here.

19:30.008 --> 19:31.009
But―

19:31.134 --> 19:32.135
SOKKA: Go!

19:32.928 --> 19:33.929
Hurry, Sokka!

19:41.395 --> 19:42.604
( BREATHING HEAVILY )

19:48.694 --> 19:50.278
What is it now?

19:58.829 --> 19:59.996
Who is there?

20:07.462 --> 20:08.880
AANG: Why are we doing this?

20:08.964 --> 20:11.967
Because if this calendar can tell us
about eclipses in the past,

20:12.050 --> 20:14.511
then maybe it can project
when the next one will be.

20:14.594 --> 20:16.596
You can't possibly
check every single date.

20:16.680 --> 20:18.765
I don't have to.
We just need to check

20:18.890 --> 20:20.892
every date before Sozin's Comet arrives,

20:20.976 --> 20:24.521
because after that,
well, try not to think about that.

20:44.583 --> 20:45.709
Come on, eclipse!

20:49.379 --> 20:51.381
SOKKA: That's it― The solar eclipse.

20:51.465 --> 20:53.175
It's just a few months away.

20:54.926 --> 20:57.179
Got it! Now let's get to Ba Sing Se.

21:15.155 --> 21:17.407
Don't make me put this down.

21:27.459 --> 21:29.795
No! Stop sinking!

21:34.257 --> 21:35.342
No!

21:36.593 --> 21:37.886
I'm sorry, Appa.

21:42.098 --> 21:43.850
-( CHATTERING )
-( SCREECHING )

21:56.863 --> 22:00.325
At least I'll have one specimen
to add to my collection.

22:00.408 --> 22:01.785
Aah!

22:11.086 --> 22:13.797
Your waterbending
won't do you much good here.

22:14.297 --> 22:17.467
I've studied northern water style,
southern water style,

22:17.551 --> 22:20.136
even foggy swamp style.

22:21.304 --> 22:23.932
Hyah!

22:25.976 --> 22:28.854
That's called Sokka style. Learn it.

22:35.026 --> 22:37.529
Wait! Professor, let's go.

22:37.946 --> 22:40.407
I'm not leaving. I can't.

22:40.490 --> 22:43.118
I've spent too long
trying to find this place.

22:43.368 --> 22:45.370
There's not
another collection of knowledge

22:45.453 --> 22:46.580
like this on earth.

22:47.998 --> 22:50.458
I could spend an eternity in here.

22:50.917 --> 22:51.960
Just go!

22:52.043 --> 22:54.754
( WAN SHI TONG SCREECHES )

22:55.630 --> 22:56.673
( KIDS SCREAMING )

23:20.071 --> 23:22.741
We got it.
There's a solar eclipse coming.

23:22.824 --> 23:24.659
The Fire Nation's in trouble now.

23:27.621 --> 23:29.289
Where's Appa?
